<edge source="strait_of_hormuz::oil_price_level" target="global_energy_security::capital_allocation_balan" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher sustained oil prices increase free cash flow, prompting many upstream and integrated companies to reallocate toward shareholder distributions (dividends/buybacks) and debt repayment rather than near-term growth capex.</data>
  <data key="d37">3-12 months</data>
  <data key="d38">strait_of_hormuz</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_security</data>
</edge>
<edge source="strait_of_hormuz::oil_price_level" target="monetary_currency_shift::monetary_policy_stance" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained increases in global oil prices feed into headline inflation and inflation expectations, compelling central banks to adopt tighter policy stances (higher rates or hawkish guidance) to maintain inflation targets.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">strait_of_hormuz</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_currency_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="strait_of_hormuz::oil_price_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::interceptor_stocks" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in global oil prices increases Russian export revenues and budget space for munitions procurement and production, which sustains higher rates of Russian missile/drone employment and thus accelerates Ukrainian interceptor expenditure, depleting interceptor inventories.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">strait_of_hormuz</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="strait_of_hormuz::oil_price_level" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_dc_investment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained increases in oil and fuel prices raise electricity/fuel operating costs and project discount rates for hyperscalers and enterprises, making capital‑intensive AI and data‑center builds less economically attractive and slowing new investment commitments.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">strait_of_hormuz</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
