<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::interceptor_stocks" target="global_energy_security::capital_allocation_balan" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher inventories of interceptors reduce near‑term compulsory defensive spending by governments and asset owners, freeing free cash flow to be allocated back to dividends, buybacks or debt repayment rather than urgent procurement, shifting capital allocation toward shareholder returns.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_security</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::interceptor_stocks" target="strait_of_hormuz::crude_export_flow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Drawdown of interceptor missile inventories due to re‑supply for Ukraine reduces available defensive coverage for tankers and export infrastructure in the Gulf, increasing successful attacks and temporary closures that lower crude export volumes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">strait_of_hormuz</data>
</edge>
