<edge source="global_energy_security::operating_margin_level" target="monetary_currency_shift::monetary_policy_stance" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in energy-sector operating margins (from supply tightness or price spikes) passes quickly into headline inflation and producer pricing power, prompting central banks to tighten policy stance to contain inflation.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_security</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_currency_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_security::operating_margin_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::critical_infra_vuln" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher operating margins enable energy firms to fund near‑term maintenance, cybersecurity and physical hardening of pipelines, terminals and grids, reducing those assets' susceptibility to drone strikes and functional loss.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_security</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_security::operating_margin_level" target="strait_of_hormuz::crude_export_flow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising operating margins make marginal and higher-cost wells commercially viable and reduce shut-ins, increasing production available for export, while margin compression prompts producers to curtail output and reduce shipments.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_security</data>
  <data key="d39">strait_of_hormuz</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_security::operating_margin_level" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_dc_investment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.78</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher operating margins at energy‑intensive cloud and AI providers (driven by improved energy security/lower energy costs) free internal cash and reduce the need to cut capex, causing firms to proceed with planned AI hardware purchases and data‑center projects.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_security</data>
