<edge source="monetary_currency_shift::exchange_rate_level" target="global_energy_security::operating_margin_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A stronger US dollar (appreciation in exchange_rate_level versus local currencies) raises the local-currency cost of dollar-priced crude and imported inputs for non‑US refiners/importers, increasing COGS and squeezing operating margins quickly.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">monetary_currency_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_security</data>
</edge>
<edge source="monetary_currency_shift::exchange_rate_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::critical_infra_vuln" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An appreciation of the domestic currency (higher exchange_rate_level) lowers the local cost of imported spare parts, protective hardware and contracted services, enabling faster repairs and hardening of energy/logistics assets and thereby reducing critical infrastructure vulnerability.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">monetary_currency_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="monetary_currency_shift::exchange_rate_level" target="strait_of_hormuz::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A significant depreciation of the US dollar component of exchange_rate_level raises dollar-priced oil costs for non‑USD buyers and typically bids up crude prices as markets adjust for currency-driven demand and hedging flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">monetary_currency_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">strait_of_hormuz</data>
</edge>
<edge source="monetary_currency_shift::exchange_rate_level" target="strait_of_hormuz::disruption_sentiment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp depreciation of importers' currencies (changes in exchange_rate_level) can impair buyers' ability to settle dollar invoices on time, producing payment delays and contractual shipment hold-ups that raise market expectations of Strait transit disruptions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">monetary_currency_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">strait_of_hormuz</data>
</edge>
<edge source="monetary_currency_shift::exchange_rate_level" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::advanced_chip_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A depreciation of a purchaser's currency versus the USD increases the local cost of USD‑priced advanced fab equipment and materials, prompting delays or reductions in planned advanced semiconductor fabs.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">monetary_currency_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
